course: dictionary
lesson: 5968
title: Mature: more than just old
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mature has more than one meaning, so the clues around it tell you which one to use. «The mature oak tree» is a tree that is fully grown. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Full-grown fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «She made a mature decision to say sorry.» Here mature describes behaviour. A mature person is sensible and grown-up, the way an adult might act. Swap in sensible and read the sentence again. It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Mature can also be a verb, meaning to grow up or become ready: «cheese matures with time». Sometimes mature is a soft way of saying older, as in «mature students». When you are unsure, put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Mature means fully grown or developed.
fact: Mature can describe behaviour: a mature person is sensible and grown-up.
fact: As a verb, mature means to grow up or become ready, like cheese that matures with time.
fact: Advertisers may say «mature students» instead of «old students», because it sounds nicer. A soft word used in place of a plainer one is called a euphemism.
fact: Add the prefix im- to mature and you get immature: im + mature = immature.
exercise: «The mature oak tree stood at the edge of the field.» What does mature mean here? | Brand new | *Fully grown | Painted green | Very small
exercise: «She made a mature decision to say sorry.» What does mature suggest about her? | *Sensible and grown-up | Silly and loud | Late and lost | Happy and noisy
exercise: Fill the gap: «Cheese needs time to ___ and become tasty.» | shrink | freeze | *mature | sing
test: In the USA, a game with ESRB M on the box is rated for about 17 and up. What does M stand for? | Monster | Mini | Music | *Mature
test: Advertisers say «mature students» instead of «old students». What is this kind of soft, nicer word called? | A prefix | *A euphemism | A verb | A synonym
exam: Add im- to mature to make the word for not sensible or not grown-up. Which word is it? | *Immature | Matured | Maturity | Unmature
